       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no protocol or indication that supports it. The risk of serious harm is high: serotonin syndrome, seizures, arrhythmia. This is a decision I can't make for you, and I don't want to put an order into the system that could reach the patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **A dose within the labeled range.** Give me the dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **A different clinical goal.** If you're trying to treat refractory symptoms, I can help you think through other options. These include optimizing to 200 mg, augmentation, switching agents, or a psychiatry consult.\n- **A truly unusual plan.** If there is a specific rationale, talk with your attending and pharmacy first. Once the dose is approved and documented, it can be entered through the appropriate channel.\n\nIf the 1000 mg came from a transcription error, a mix-up with another drug, or a unit mistake, I can help you sort that out."
      }
